Item Number:  SCP-5134

Object Class:  Safe

Special Containment Procedures:  SCP-5134 is to be kept in a locked container with no air ducts/vents anywhere inside of the containment cell. Personnel are authorized to enter SCP-5134's containment cell, but must be wearing airtight hazmat suits at all times while inside SCP-5134's containment cell.

Description:  SCP-5134 appears to be a large jar filled with sliced pickles and pickle juice. SCP-5134's lid appears to be a standard pickle jar lid, apart from the fact that no known living being has the strength to remove the lid from the jar. However when any piece of technology such as a prosthetic arm is used to attempt to remove the lid from the jar, the jar is removed with just as much effort as it would take to remove the lid from a non-anomalous pickle jar.

During a test with an amputee foundation personnel equipped with a prosthetic arm, the foundation personnel removed the lid from the jar and quantities of a gas substance emitted from the jar. All personnel that were located within SCP-5134's containment cell passed out shortly after the gas began to emit from the jar. All personnel regained consciousness approximately 2-3 hours later, reported to have minor headaches and dizziness.

The gas that emits from SCP-5134 is believed to emit from the pickle juice inside of the jar, however it is not known whether the pickles inside of the jar are anomalous or not.

                    

                                    





            
    

                    



                    
                        
                            
